---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_386",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 386,
  "text": "[[1661.9]] <b>327₂.  Origo veritatum contingentium ex processu in infinitum\n [[1661.17]] <b>Origo veritatum contingentium ex processu in infinitum</b>\n [[1661.18]] <b>ad exemplum proportionum inter quantitates incommensurabiles</b>\n[[1661.19]] <tab/><k>Veritas</k> <tab/><k>Proportio</k>\n [[1661.20]] est, inesse\n [[1661.21]] praedicatum subjecto, <tab/>quantitatem minorem majori vel\n [[1661.22]] <tab/>aequalem aequali,\n [[1661.23]] ostenditur\n [[1661.24]] reddendo rationem <tab/>explicando habitudinem\n [[1661.25]] per analysin terminorum in communes utrique\n [[1661.26]] notiones. <tab/>quantitates.\n [[1662.1]] Haec Analysis vel finita est, vel infinita.\n [[1662.2]] Si finita sit, dicitur\n [[1662.3]] Demonstratio. <tab/>Inventio communis mensurae seu\n [[1662.4]] <tab/>commensuratio.\n [[1662.5]] Et veritas est necessaria. <tab/>Et proportio est effabilis.\n [[1662.6]] Reducitur enim ad\n [[1662.7]] veritates identicas <tab/><tab/>congruentiam cum mensura eadem repetita\n [[1662.8]] seu ad principium primum\n [[1662.9]] contradictionis sive identitatis. <tab/>aequalitatis eorum quae congruunt.\n [[1662.10]] Sin Analysis procedat in infinitum\n [[1662.11]] nec unquam perveniatur ad exhaustionem\n [[1662.12]] veritas est contingens <tab/>proportio est ineffabilis\n [[1662.13]] quae infinitas involvit rationes <tab/>quae infinitos habet quotientes\n [[1662.14]] ita tamen ut semper aliquod sit residuum\n [[1662.15]] cujus iterum reddenda sit ratio <tab/>novum praebens quotientem\n [[1662.16]] continuata autem analysi prodit series infinita\n [[1662.17]] quae tamen a Deo perfecte cognoscitur. <tab/>circa quam Geometra multa cognoscit.\n [[1662.18]] Et haec est\n [[1662.19]] scientia visionis <tab/>Doctrina de numeris surdis\n [[1662.20]] <tab/>qualis est Decimo <i>Elementorum</i> contenta\n [[1662.21]] distincta\n [[1662.22]] a scientia simplicis intelligentiae <tab/>ab Arithmetica communi\n [[1662.23]] utraque tamen non experimentalis, sed a priori habens infallibilitatem,\n [[1662.24]] et secundum quidem genus\n [[1662.25]] per rationes certas, <tab/>per demonstrationes necessarias\n [[1663.1]] uni Deo infinitum comprehendenti <tab/>Geometrae cognitas, numeris tamen\n [[1663.2]] perspectas, non necessarias tamen <tab/>effabilibus non comprehendendas\n [[1663.3]] nam\n [[1663.4]] demonstrationes veritatum <tab/>proportiones surdas arithmetice cognosci\n [[1663.5]] contingentium dari <tab/>seu per mensurae repetitionem explicari\n [[1663.6]] impossibile est. </p>\n<p> [[1663.7]] Veritates contingentes dari, in quarum rationibus reddendis processus in infinitum\n[[1663.8]] fiat, vel hinc intelligitur, quod infinitae sunt actu creaturae in qualibet parte universi; et\n[[1663.9]] unaquaeque substantia individualis in notione sua completa totam seriem rerum involvit,\n[[1663.10]] et cum aliis omnibus consentit adeoque aliquid infiniti continet. Quod non intellectum\n[[1663.11]] fecit etiam ut Unio animae et corporis inexplicabilis haberetur; neque enim in se invicem\n[[1663.12]] influunt in Metaphysico rigore, imo nec Deus unius occasione aliud movet et a suo\n[[1663.13]] proprio cursu deturbat; sed unumquodque suas leges prosequens ex primaevae institutionis\n[[1663.14]] admiranda sed infallibili directione tam exacte alteri consentit, ac si verus esset\n[[1663.15]] influxus. Estque aliquid simile in omnibus substantiis etiam a se invicem remotissimis.\n[[1663.16]] Etsi in illis consensus non ita distincte appareat. </p>\n<p> [[1663.17]] Si omne quod fit, necessarium esset sequeretur sola quae aliquando existunt esse\n[[1663.18]] possibilia (ut volunt Hobbes et Spinosa) et materiam omnes formas possibiles suscipere\n[[1663.19]] (quod volebat Cartesius). Ita nullus fingi posset Romaniscus, qui non aliquando aut\n[[1664.1]] alicubi existeret. Quod absurdum est. Itaque potius dicemus ex infinitis seriebus possibilibus\n[[1664.2]] unam elegisse Deum, propter rationes captum creaturarum superantes. </p>\n<p> [[1664.3]] Causa mali est a limitatione originali creaturarum ante omne peccatum; nec a Deo\n[[1664.4]] decernitur, nisi id solummodo quod pure positivum est, seu in perfectione consistit, et\n[[1664.5]] ideo malum permittitur tantum a Deo; quod secus est in hominibus qui per se ad majus\n[[1664.6]] bonum generale non tendunt. </p>\n<p> [[1664.7]] Omnis veritas quae identica non est, probationem recipit; necessaria ostendendo\n[[1664.8]] contrarium implicare contradictionem; contingens ostendendo plus rationis esse pro eo\n[[1664.9]] quod factum est quam pro opposito. Nam ut sapientis ita et Dei primum decretum sive\n[[1664.10]] propositum est omnia agere cum summa ratione. Ita si fingeremus casum, in quo constaret\n[[1664.11]] existere debere triangulum dati ambitus, nihil vero esse in datis unde erui queat\n[[1664.12]] species Trianguli, dicendum erit a Deo triangulum aequilaterum, libere quidem, haud\n[[1664.13]] dubie tamen, productum iri. Nihil enim in datis est, quod impediat quodvis aliud existere\n[[1664.14]] triangulum, itaque aequilaterum non est necessarium. Interim ut nullum aliud eligatur\n[[1664.15]] sufficit in nullo alio praeterquam in hoc rationem esse cur caeteris praeferatur: idemque\n[[1664.16]] est si datum sit lineam a dato puncto ad punctum datum duci debere, nec quicquam datum\n[[1664.17]] quo lineae species aut magnitudo determinetur, fiet recta certo, sed libere, nam quemadmodum\n[[1664.18]] nihil est quod curvam impediat, ita et nihil quod eam suadeat. </p>\n",
  "number": "327₂.",
  "title": "Origo veritatum contingentium ex processu in infinitum",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:327₂. Origo veritatum contingentium ex processu in infinitum Origo veritatum contingentium ex processu in infinitum ad exemplum proportionum inter quantitates incommensurabiles Veritas Proportio est, inesse praedicatum subjecto, quantitatem minorem majori vel aequalem aequali, ostenditur reddendo ra...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>